// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Tabbit's data updater, for Unreal.
//
// Brings a local copy of the exported data up to date with a copy served over HTTP - a
// CDN, a bucket, a patch server - so a build can take new data without shipping a new
// one. Written beside the generated module when the recipe asks for it, and reads nothing
// but the manifest, so it knows nothing about the schema and never changes when one does.
//
// The manifest is what the exporter already writes next to the data: one entry per file
// with its size and MD5. Comparing it with the local copy is the whole of the diff, so a
// run fetches what changed and nothing else.
//
// Three properties, because a patcher that fails badly is worse than one that does not
// exist:
//
//   Nothing is replaced until everything has arrived and been checked. Files land in a
//   staging directory first and the local manifest is written last, so an update
//   interrupted halfway leaves the previous data readable and the next run redoes the
//   difference.
//
//   Every file is checked against the hash the manifest gives for it, so a truncated
//   transfer that a proxy reported as success does not reach the cache.
//
//   A transient failure is retried with a doubling backoff, and a permanent one is not.
//
// Reading is somebody else's job. This produces a directory, and the generated accessor
// reads it.
//
// The module needs "HTTP" in its dependencies. The generated Build.cs adds it when the
// updater is written.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

#pragma once

